{{!-- Kleinkram: Geld, Papiere und Krimskrams — carried gear the inventory rules
price at zero slots, so it never occupies a cell in the Trageslots raster and
gets a column of its own here instead.

The column has no create control and no drop target of its own. Nothing here is
a state a piece can be put *into*: an item is Kleinkram exactly when its
`slots` is 0, which is authored on the item's own sheet. Same interactions as a
slot cell otherwise — costing nothing to carry does not make it a different kind
of thing, so it can still be opened, sorted and worn. --}}
<div class='slot-trinkets card'>

  <div class='slot-trinkets-header'>
    {{!-- The explanation hangs off the label rather than the whole block: the
    items below carry their own tooltips, and a container-wide one only ever
    showed in the gaps between them. --}}
    <span class='slot-trinkets-title'
          data-tooltip-html='{{localize "TNO.Inventory.TrinketsHint"}}'
          data-tooltip-direction='LEFT'>{{localize 'TNO.Inventory.Trinkets'}}</span>
    <span class='slot-trinkets-cost'>{{localize 'TNO.Inventory.TrinketsZeroSlots'}}</span>
  </div>

  {{#if slotGrid.trinkets.length}}
    <div class='slot-trinkets-list'>
      {{#each slotGrid.trinkets as |trinket|}}
        <span class='slot-trinket draggable' data-item-id='{{trinket.item._id}}'
              data-tooltip-html='{{trinket.tip}}' data-tooltip-direction='UP'>
          <img src='{{trinket.item.img}}' width='14' height='14' alt=''/>
          <span class='slot-trinket-name'>{{trinket.item.name}}</span>
          {{#if trinket.showQty}}<span class='slot-qty'>×{{trinket.quantity}}</span>{{/if}}
        </span>
      {{/each}}
    </div>
  {{else}}
    <p class='slot-trinkets-empty'>{{localize 'TNO.Inventory.TrinketsEmpty'}}</p>
  {{/if}}

</div>
